urn 24, lost 10.2. GPT-6.1 Sol averaged 4.4 points lost per move to the 20k's 2.9, and the lead sank to -30.1 by the final pass.", "moments": [{"turn": 11, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol played F5 and extended its row of stones on the fifth line. The lead went from +0.8 to -7.1, a loss of 7.9. The engine preferred F3. This was the first big swing, and Black never led again."}, {"turn": 14, "text": "The 20k answered with C6 and gave the points back. The move lost 6.9, taking the lead from -7.0 to -0.1, and the engine's choice was H5. For a moment the game was level again."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "After D6 had lost 7.8 on the previous turn, D7 lost another 7.7, dropping the lead from -7.9 to -15.6. The engine's choice was H5, a move away from the left-side fight. A wall of Black stones on the D file was growing, but White was getting its points elsewhere."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 20k's B2 at turn 24 lost 10.2 and brought the lead from -20.2 to -10.1. GPT-6.1 Sol's D3 then lost 10.2 right back, to -20.2. The engine wanted E4. The one chance to get back into the game lasted exactly one move."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "E3 lost 7.7 and dropped the lead from -20.3 to -28.0, and the engine's choice was B8. Black kept filling in the lower side while White's row of stones along the fourth line stood untouched. After this the result was settled, and the last pass left it at -30.1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran works on the current position or on records: current-position-liberties.js (inspectLiberties) lists chains and their liberties, the regions function counts empty regions and their bordering colours, and the other scripts only read game notes, replay moves to build an SGF, and write notes. None of it generates, ranks or looks ahead over candidate moves; each move was passed by hand to mcp__go__play.", "stop": false}}